artifacts/track_a_scratch/ledger/** -text

# Archived execution evidence: the bytes that ran, not a normalised copy of them.
# `docs/governance/m15_track_a_r1_execution_record.md` records a sha256 for the
# R1 driver and calls it "the bytes that executed"; without this line git stores
# an LF-normalised blob on a CRLF host, so the recorded hash is unreproducible in
# a fresh clone and the only record of how an irreversible run was driven cannot
# be checked. A review role measured exactly that.
docs/governance/evidence/** -text
